\begin{definition}\label{definition:fibration}
   An operadic functor $p\colon \bP \to \bO$ is an operadic fibration if it induces a surjection $\pi_0\bP \twoheadrightarrow \pi_0\bO$ on the sets connected components, and for any $b, a_1,\ldots, a_{k} \in \bP$, with $|b|=k$, and $f\colon x \to pb$ in $\bO$ with fibers $pa_j$, there exists an operadic $p$-cartesian lift $\tilde{f}$ of $f$ in~$\bP$ with fibers~$a_j$. 
\end{definition}
